-- title:
--   An order-three automorphism acting regularly on E₀[M]
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field with decidable equality and let $M$ be a nonzero natural number whose image in $K$ is nonzero. Then there exist a Weierstrass curve $E_0$ over $K$ together with a witness that $E_0$ is elliptic, an admissible variable change $\sigma \in$ `WeierstrassCurve.VariableChange K` (given by data $u \in K^\times$ and $r, s, t \in K$), and two points $P, Q$ of the affine model of $E_0$, such that: $j(E_0) = 0$; $\sigma$ fixes the Weierstrass model, $\sigma \bullet E_0 = E_0$; $M \bullet P = 0$ and $M \bullet Q = 0$; every point $T$ of $E_0$ with $M \bullet T = 0$ is expressible as $T = c_1 \bullet P + c_2 \bullet Q$ (natural-number multiples by the canonical representatives $c_i \in \{0,\dots,M-1\}$) for a unique pair $c = (c_1, c_2) \in \mathbb{Z}/M \times \mathbb{Z}/M$; and, writing `Point.vcInvFun` for the map $E_0 \to \sigma \bullet E_0$ sending $0$ to $0$ and an affine point $(x,y)$ to $(u^{-2}(x - r),\, u^{-3}(y - t - s(x - r)))$, one has the heterogeneous equalities `Point.vcInvFun` $\sigma\, E_0\, P = Q$ and `Point.vcInvFun` $\sigma\, E_0\, Q = -P - Q$ (heterogeneous because the source and target point types are identified only through $\sigma \bullet E_0 = E_0$).
--
--   This is the "regular module" property of the $M$-torsion of the curve with $j = 0$: an automorphism of order three acts on the basis $(P,Q)$ of $E_0[M] \cong (\mathbb{Z}/M)^2$ by the matrix $\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 1 \\ -1 & -1\end{pmatrix}$, so that $E_0[M]$ is free of rank one over $\mathbb{Z}[X]/(M, X^2 + X + 1)$ with generator $P$. It is used in the analysis of the fibre of the modular curve above $j = 0$, where points are counted by double cosets modulo the subgroup generated by the image of this matrix, in [`ModularCurve.exists_injective_doubleCoset_forall_diamondPullbackModL_smul_place_eq_of_ord_pos`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_injective_doubleCoset_forall_diamondPullbackModL_smul_place_eq_of_ord_pos).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_exists_j_eq_zero_torsion_basis_heq_vcInvFun_of_order_three.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_WeierstrassCurve_VariableChangePointEquiv

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open WeierstrassCurve WeierstrassCurve.Affine

theorem WeierstrassCurve.exists_j_eq_zero_torsion_basis_heq_vcInvFun_of_order_three
    (K : Type*) [Field K] [DecidableEq K] [IsAlgClosed K] (M : ℕ) [NeZero M] (hM : (M : K) ≠ 0) :
    ∃ (E₀ : WeierstrassCurve K) (_ : E₀.IsElliptic) (σ : WeierstrassCurve.VariableChange K)
      (P Q : E₀.toAffine.Point),
      E₀.j = 0 ∧ σ • E₀ = E₀ ∧ M • P = 0 ∧ M • Q = 0 ∧
      (∀ T : E₀.toAffine.Point, M • T = 0 →
        ∃! c : ZMod M × ZMod M, T = c.1.val • P + c.2.val • Q) ∧
      HEq (Point.vcInvFun σ E₀.toAffine P) Q ∧
      HEq (Point.vcInvFun σ E₀.toAffine Q) (-P - Q) := by sorry
